      "title": "The whole system",
      "legend": true,
      "caption": "<strong>Read it top to bottom.</strong> Requests come through one load balancer. Go <code>api/common</code> handles everything, including authorizing each upload and handing the app a signed ticket for it. Photos then go to the Node gateway, which accepts nothing without a ticket and passes only pointers onward. Below the Kafka bar, the Python service makes every decision and sends it back for Go to save. The dotted grey line is telemetry.",
      "diagram": {
        "width": 1200,
