        "aria": "Ledgerline architecture. Browsers and the mobile app reach one load balancer, which sends ticketed uploads to api/intake (Node gateway) and everything else to api/common (Go, CRUD). api/common is the only client of Postgres and uses Redis for rate limits. The gateway puts photos in temporary Cloud Storage and hands pointers to Kafka. api/process (Python) parses and categorizes receipts and sends results back through Kafka. All three services send telemetry to the observability gateway.",
